  "compositions": [
    {
      "name": "nu",
      "path": "nu/",
      "prompt_texts": {
        "1a286812ed6230e4c6c0c8d7d54720a8a060b62da39e7685e2e22bfe5ed337d1": "# nu - prompt 007\n\n<!-- recorded: 2026-11-15T18:57:15Z; source: user -->\n\nAdd a breathy, windy pad alongside the existing pad, in the same harmony but on a different voice of the chord.\n",
        "1ea933beb578fed7d1f3a5274ed8f05fb2357fd8f6ee71cde5bda9af08136f8d": "# nu - prompt 004\n\n<!-- recorded: 2026-11-15T18:33:13Z; source: user -->\n\nviewer submit smoke test\n",
        "579fed5dd7813a1355e62921e84f5060c802790fc7a20bfa0c6e7940e2fcbff4": "# nu - prompt 003\n\n<!-- recorded: 2026-11-14T14:35:48Z; source: agent -->\n\nDemonstration prompt, written by the implementing agent (Claude) to exercise the studio; it is not a prompt from Michael Gogins.\n\nRevise the generator. Answer the bell melody with a canon: the same melody four scale steps higher (a diatonic fifth, staying in D Dorian), two seconds later, softer, farther away, and on the opposite side. Let the melody range more widely than before. Make the drone a little softer so the two bell voices stay clear.\n",
        "750acd16db5c806deea5f0660c2c78ecc903ce5545750b6ab98dd306f8b66331": "# nu - prompt 006\n\n<!-- recorded: 2026-11-15T18:51:37Z; source: user -->\n\nExtend the process in version 3 at the same tempo for piece 2 minutes long.\n",
        "9541e095bf039cc2a82a02f4d3b80b4f3a218fc4288c83a2b3caf97d8d903054": "# nu - prompt 001\n\n<!-- recorded: 2026-11-14T14:35:45Z; source: agent -->\n\nDemonstration prompt, written by the implementing agent (Claude) to exercise the studio; it is not a prompt from Michael Gogins.\n\nCompose a very short study called nu, about 18 seconds long: a slow, bell-like melody in D Dorian over a low drone, with reverberation. Write it directly as one complete Csound .csd file, with the instruments and the notes, using the studio p-field conventions (p4 MIDI key, p5 MIDI velocity, p6 depth, p7 pan).\n",
        "ca4c3922c0f22aba2f7b10c6a4b4959091a87b1ce1c93298fadc71ef3511c53d": "# nu - prompt 002\n\n<!-- recorded: 2026-11-14T14:35:46Z; source: agent -->\n\nDemonstration prompt, written by the implementing agent (Claude) to exercise the studio; it is not a prompt from Michael Gogins.\n\nKeep the instruments of nu exactly as they are, but stop writing the notes by hand. Generate the score with a Python program that uses CsoundAC: the bells play a seeded random walk on the D Dorian scale with irregular rhythm, moving between left and right; the drone on D is joined by its fifth halfway through. Keep the program beside the piece so that the .csd can be regenerated from it, and record the random seed.\n",
        "f94031cf4dfb7f47533db6df04cfa534892461f57fc1d4a700c405652a4ae3a1": "# nu - prompt 005\n\n<!-- recorded: 2026-11-15T18:38:44Z; source: user -->\n\nExtend the process in version 3 but at the same tempo to make the piece 2 minutes long.\n"
      },
      "title": "Nu (studio demonstration)",
